AB  - Abstract The present study developed a 12-item Big Three Perfectionism Scale (BTPS-12) among 468 adolescents. The tri-angle translation approach was used to obtain the Chinese version and avoid semantic understanding differences bought by different languages. Both theory and data-driven (e.g., exploratory structural equation modeling) approaches were employed to construct the short form. The same three-global-factor structure was established. Pearson correlation coefficients between the original version and the short form, as well as their associations with negative emotion symptoms and flourishing indicated criterion-related validities. Comparable explained variances in mental health outcomes were also identified using hierarchical regressions between the original version and the short form.
